    {
      "id": "e02",
      "section": "why_midsurface",
      "narration": "To analyze a thin metal part, solvers split it into fine mesh blocks. Thin walls force tiny blocks, so solves turn slow. We replace a thin solid with one middle surface called a midsurface. One clean shell needs far fewer blocks and cuts the number of solver hours down.",
      "budget_s": [
        19,
        22
      ],
      "facts": [],
      "visual": {
        "kind": "manim",
        "template": "why_midsurface",
